'''''Portulaca umbraticola''''', also known as the '''wingpod purslane''', is an annual or short-lived perennial [[Succulent plant|succulent]] in the genus of flowering plants ''[[Portulaca]]''.  Native to the New World, it is now found as a garden plant in the Old World due to its ornamental nature.

== Description ==
Although this species can be easily mistaken for ''[[Portulaca oleracea|P. oleracea]]'', its foliage tends to be much smaller and wider than that of other species. Flower colours range from yellow, pink, and orange. The entire plant including the stems, leaves, flowers and roots are all edible. Plants grow up to 25&nbsp;cm tall.<ref>{{cite web|title=Portulaca umbraticola – Wingpod Purslane|url=https://worldofsucculents.com/portulaca-umbraticola-wingpod-purslane/|website=World of Succulents}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Wingpod Purslane|url=http://www.flowersofindia.net/catalog/slides/Wingpod%20Purslane.html|website=Flowers of India}}</ref>

==Subspecies==
Three subspecies are recognized: ''P. u. coronata'', ''P. u. lanceolata'', and the nominate ''P. u. umbraticola''.<ref>{{Catalogue of Life |1f0d33f376bcd26fb31556adefb1c48e }}</ref>

